# MI Gas — every variable the site reads. Copy to .env.local for local work; set the real
# values in the hosting dashboard. Never commit a filled-in copy of this file.
#
# House rule, and the reason this file exists: nothing here is a paid service. Mail goes
# over SMTP through a mailbox the client already owns. There is no scheduling account, no
# object store and no mail API, so there is nothing on this list that can send him a bill.

# ── Mail ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset SMTP_HOST and the site still works — forms succeed for the visitor and the full
# brief is written to the server log. That is deliberate (a form that errors because of a
# missing env var teaches people it is broken) and it means bookings exist ONLY in the log
# until this is set. Set it before anyone real uses the site.
SMTP_HOST=
# 587 for STARTTLS, 465 for implicit TLS. The code switches `secure` on this number;
# getting it backwards fails by hanging rather than by erroring.
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
# Must be an address that mailbox is allowed to send as. Falls back to SMTP_USER.
SMTP_FROM=

# ── Where enquiries land ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Falls back to SITE.email in lib/site.ts, which is still a PLACEHOLDER — so until one of
# the two is real, notification is skipped and logged.
MIGAS_NOTIFY_TO=
